  "problem": "In this lesson, we'll extend our knowledge of absolute value. \n\nLet's first remind ourselves of the rules of absolute value:\n\n- $|{-a}| = |a|$\n\n- $|a \\cdot b| = |a| \\cdot |b|$\n\n- $\\left| \\dfrac{a}{b} \\right| = \\dfrac{|a|}{|b|}$\n\nRecall that the last two rules are known as the **distributive properties.**",
